Suggests: ffmpeg
Description: Zero-copy C23 Wayland wallpaper, VA-API video, Shadertoy, and Material You engine
 wwal (WayWal) is a high-performance Wayland wallpaper daemon (wwald) and
 client (wwal) written in C23. It provides direct DMA-BUF scanout, 18 GLES 3.1
 compute shader transitions, zero-FFmpeg VA-API hardware video playback, live
 Shadertoy shaders with PipeWire 64-bin Bark FFT audio reactivity, Zero-Watt
 smart occlusion/battery governance, and sub-millisecond OKLab/CAM16/HCT
 Material Design 3 color extraction.
